hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2865","Narrated to us Abu Musa and Salam ibn Junadah (RA): They both said: Narrated to us Abu Mu'awiyah (RA), who narrated to us al-A'mash (RA).\n\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar (RA), who narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adi (RA), from Shu'bah (RA), from Sulayman—who is al-A'mash (RA)—from Muslim al-Batin (RA), from Sa'id ibn Jubayr (RA), from Ibn 'Abbas (RA), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah than these days"",""\"" meaning the days of the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah.\n\nThey asked"","" \""Not even jihad in the cause of Allah?\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) replied"","" \""Not even jihad in the cause of Allah"","" except for a man who goes out with his life and his wealth and does not return with anything from it.\""\n\nThis is the narration of Abu Mu'awiyah (RA).\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
